#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
netui — a full curses front-end for NetworkManager (Wi-Fi / Ethernet / VPN /
Mobile / PPPoE), in the spirit of bluetui.

Features
--------
  * Tabs: Wi-Fi, Ethernet, VPN, Mobile & DSL, Adapters, Profiles
  * Two-pane layout: list on the left, details for the selected item on the right
  * All nmcli calls run on a background thread — the UI never blocks
  * Connect/disconnect, rescan, hidden networks, forget a saved network
  * Create connections:
      - VPN: PPTP, L2TP/IPsec, OpenVPN (import), WireGuard (import),
             OpenConnect, vpnc, SSTP, Fortinet SSL — depending on which
             NetworkManager VPN plugin is actually installed
      - Mobile: GSM (APN/PIN), CDMA
      - PPPoE (DSL / dial-up-over-Ethernet)
  * Edit a profile: name, autoconnect, IPv4 (auto/manual), DNS, IPv6
  * Wi-Fi/WWAN radio toggle, event log, in-app key reference
  * Adapters tab: raw `nmcli device status` view, so you can see exactly
    which physical/virtual network devices the system actually has

Dependencies: Python 3.8+ stdlib (curses) and nmcli only.
ModemManager (mmcli) is optional, used for operator/signal info if present.

Run: chmod +x netui.py && ./netui.py
Keys: press "?" inside the app.
"""

